course: dictionary
lesson: 14819
title: Words for feeling sick or uneasy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how your body feels. Queasy is one of them. When you feel queasy, your stomach is unhappy and you think you might be sick. «After the bumpy boat ride, Sam felt queasy and had to sit down.» The bumpy boat is the clue. It tells you the queasy feeling came from the movement.
explain: Queasy can also describe a worried feeling inside you, not your stomach. «Mia had a queasy feeling before her spelling test.» Mia is not ill. She is nervous. The word test is the clue that tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. Ask: is this about my body, or about how I feel about something? Then swap in a simple word, such as sick or uneasy, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Queasy means feeling a little sick in your stomach, as if you might vomit.
fact: Queasy can also mean uneasy or uncomfortable about something.
fact: The noun is queasiness: «The queasiness passed after Sam got off the boat.»
fact: Travel, a bug, or eating too much can make you feel queasy.
fact: A good check is to swap in sick or uneasy and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «After the bumpy boat ride, Sam felt queasy.» What does queasy mean here? | Feeling very tired and sleepy | Feeling very excited and full of energy | Feeling cold and wet | *Feeling a little sick in the stomach
exercise: «Mia had a queasy feeling before her spelling test.» What does queasy suggest here? | *Uneasy and nervous about something | Loud and cheerful | Hungry for lunch | Happy and relaxed
exercise: Find and copy the noun form of queasy. | feeling | stomach | queasy | *queasiness
test: «Ben ate too much cake and now has a queasy stomach.» Which word is closest in meaning to queasy? | happy | tired | *sick | loud
test: Which sentence uses queasy to mean uneasy? | We ate queasy biscuits at lunch. | *Nervous about the speech, Lily had a queasy feeling all morning. | The queasy boat rocked gently on the lake. | The sea was calm, so Tom felt fine.
exam: Which word means the same as queasy in a story about nerves? | sleepy | loud | *uneasy | cheerful
